 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55", "title": "[P3] The board-lint pre-commit hook installed in this repo is INERT: a global core.hooksPath (/home/kara/.hermes/hooks) overrides $GIT_DIR/hooks, so git never runs .git/hooks/pre-commit \u2014 the board's duplicate-id / dangling-dep gate is dead in exactly the checkout that advertises it (BT-053-ROLLOUT row)", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "DOGFOOD 2026-10-20 (run 19) \u2014 found while landing this run's own commit, verified by git's own\npath resolution (no experiment needed).\n\nEVIDENCE:\n  $ git config --get core.hooksPath\n    /home/kara/.hermes/hooks\n  $ git rev-parse --git-path hooks/pre-commit\n    /home/kara/.hermes/hooks/pre-commit        <-- what git actually consults\n  $ ls -l .git/hooks/pre-commit\n    -rwxr-xr-x ... .git/hooks/pre-commit      <-- carries the boardctl board-lint managed block\n  $ head -30 /home/kara/.hermes/hooks/pre-commit\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash ... REPO_ROOT=... ; /home/kara/gitreins/.venv/bin/python -m gitreins guard; exit $?\n    (no chaining to $GIT_DIR/hooks/pre-commit)\n  $ git commit -F <msg>   # this run's commit a2784353, docs+board only\n    guard log: .gitreins/logs/guard-20261020T111645.392968Z.log -> secrets clean, go_build/go_tests skipped\n    (the gitreins guard ran; no board-lint step exists in the effective hook at all)\n\nMECHANISM: when core.hooksPath is set, git looks for hooks ONLY there \u2014 $GIT_DIR/hooks is ignored. So the\nboard-lint hook that `boardctl install` wrote into .git/hooks (recorded as complete by\nBT-053-ROLLOUT-2026-09-28, \"board-lint pre-commit hook: installed\") never executes in this checkout, and\nneither would any other repo-local hook the fleet installs. The board's own protection against duplicate\nids / dangling depends_on (the tick contract calls a duplicate id a board-lint ERROR that blocks EVERY\ncommit in the repo) is therefore inert exactly where it is advertised as installed.\n\nIMPACT: a duplicate-id or dangling-dep commit from any lane writing this board sails through; the failure\nsurfaces later as a repo-wide commit block or as a silently unreachable row. Nothing reports the gap \u2014\n`boardctl validate` is a manual/CI invocation, not a commit gate, and the effective hook prints nothing\nabout the board.\n\nNOTE (not a claim about boardctl's intent): the global hook is a fleet-wide install, so the same\noverride applies to every repo in the fleet that boardctl installed into.", "fix_direction": "Fix lives in boardctl's install path (cross-project: this board only records it).\n`boardctl install` must write the board-lint block into the EFFECTIVE hook path \u2014 resolve it with\n`git rev-parse --git-path hooks/pre-commit` (or install the block where core.hooksPath points and chain the\nrepo's own hooks from there) \u2014 and must detect the override at install time and either adapt or fail with a\nnamed remedy instead of reporting a successful install. Acceptance: in a repo whose core.hooksPath is set\nglobally, a commit that introduces a duplicate task id (or a dangling depends_on) is still BLOCKED, or the\ninstall names the override and refuses to claim success. Add the case to boardctl's own install test.", "capability_tags": ["board", "process", "tooling", "dogfood"], "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-20T11:17:39Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T11:17:39Z", "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "Fix owner is the boardctl / board-lint install path, not this project's Go code; this board row exists so the finding is not lost. Cross-checked during run 19 while committing the run's own docs+board changes (commit a2784353).", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "completed_at": null, "blocked_since": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "a3e4aaa77c1ce9a2725185c0fb6cbfe4f8cd51aa8da339c288078f72ee78800e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-20-run19", "ts": "2026-10-20T11:17:39Z"}], "ch_trace": "ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55 spec=BT-053-ROLLOUT-2026-09-28 witness=live:git-rev-parse verdict=FAIL evidence=docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-deploy-truth-integration.md"}, "acceptance_criteria": "grep -n 'boardctl_lint_mode=\"warn\"' .git/hooks/pre-commit exits 1 after the fix; today it exits 0 because lint_mode is warn and duplicate ids only WARN. | In a throwaway clone of this repo (never this checkout), append a second tasks.jsonl row whose id duplicates an existing row, stage it, and run git commit: expected outcome is that the commit is rejected \u2014 the pre-commit hook exits non-zero, git rev-parse HEAD is unchanged, and the hook output names the duplicated id. (AC migrated here from DF-OFF-BY-ONE-56, where the 2026-10-21 acceptance pass misfiled it.)"}
 {"id": "QA-OFF-BY-ONE-2-R2", "title": "[P3] RECURRENCE of QA-OFF-BY-ONE-2 \u2014 fresh-agent ci-pass FAILED on BOTH arms for env reasons (native: 'package testing is not in std' in the provisioned GOROOT -> 15 packages [setup failed]; act: the agent's rootless dockerd never started, 'No such image: catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest') \u2014 non-reproducible: same agent re-run rc=0, sibling agent same sha ci-pass OK, control host green", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "QA LANE off-by-one-qa, tick off-by-one-qa-2026-10-21-11-14-40 \u2014 FULL clean-machine battery on a JIT bunker agent (bunker-mvp, agent 9e9c0fe9, TTL 4h), evidence /home/kara/.hermes/qa/evidence/off-by-one-qa-2026-10-21-11-14-40/qa-evidence.jsonl (22 agent rows) + per-cell logs harvested BEFORE collect.\n\nRECURRENCE. QA-OFF-BY-ONE-2 (closed 2026-09-18 with foreman_note \"PREMISE-FALSE ... the act leg's failure was the harness docker environment (image absent / sandbox ENOSPC), not the workflow\") has returned in the same shape on a different agent, this time with a named, agent-local root cause for BOTH arms.\n\nTESTED HEAD: 05fa2e69ca6bfd5e284befe29177f4a84298a099 == origin/master (ls-remote refs/heads/master == 05fa2e69; the sync note \"clone dirty \u2014 pull skipped, testing recorded sha\" comes from the board/.gitreins metadata edits in the control checkout, not from a stale sha).\n\nCELL (verbatim from the agent's own evidence row):\n  {\"cell\":\"ci-pass\",\"status\":\"FAIL\",\"detail\":\"native rc=1: FAIL github.com/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one/internal/muster [setup failed]|... internal/sandbox | internal/seed | internal/solver | internal/tools | internal/web | pkg/api [setup failed]|FAIL| (act leg rc=1: No such image: catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest ...)\"}\n  native.log per-package cause (harvested from ~/qa-logs-3613902/native.log):\n    cmd/off-by-one/dispatch_test.go:14:2: package testing is not in std (/home/bunker-9e9c0fe9/tools/go/src/testing)\n    internal/api/handlers_test.go:12:2: package net/http/httptest is not in std (/home/bunker-9e9c0fe9/tools/go/src/net/http/httptest)\n  i.e. the leg's GOROOT (the toolchain-bootstrap-provisioned ~/tools/go, go1.27.3) did not carry the std test packages AT CELL TIME, so every package with a test file failed at compile time. 16 packages reported, 15 [setup failed] + 3 no-test-files.\n  ci.log (act arm): 6 jobs each logged \"docker pull image=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest forcePull=true\" then \"failed to create container: 'Error response from daemon: No such image: catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest'\" \u2192 \"Failure - Set up job\".\n\nENV-CLASS, NOT A PRODUCT DEFECT \u2014 three independent counter-surfaces on the SAME sha:\n 1. SAME agent, SAME tree, 6 minutes later: the ci-pass leg's exact command reproduced by hand \u2014\n    `( timeout -k 30 900 env PATH=\"$HOME/tools/go/bin:$PATH\" go test ./... -count=1 )` \u2192 rc=0, 16/16 packages ok\n    (cmd/off-by-one 6.299s ... pkg/api 0.198s). go env GOROOT = /home/bunker-9e9c0fe9/tools/go, go1.27.3, and\n    ~/tools/go/src/testing now exists with its full file set (77 std dirs). So the toolchain state that reddened the\n    cell did not persist; the failure is not reproducible.\n 2. SIBLING AGENT in the SAME WINDOW, same sha: a second off-by-one battery (agent 0d6df5a6, launched 11:24:58Z,\n    evidence /tmp/bunker-qa-evidence-off-by-one-20261021-qa.jsonl) graded ci-pass OK \"native suite PASS\" and its act\n    leg actually executed CI jobs (Main Checkout success 8.8s, Set up Go running). Two agents, one repo, one sha:\n    one red, one green \u21d2 agent-local environment.\n 3. CONTROL HOST at the same HEAD 05fa2e69: go build ./... rc=0, go vet ./... rc=0, go test ./... -count=1 rc=0\n    (all 16 packages ok, loadavg 10.73) \u2014 /home/kara/.hermes/qa/evidence/off-by-one-qa-2026-10-21-11-14-40/local/controlhost-suite.log.\nGCONTEXT: the battery's chaos-resource cell on the SAME agent ran the SAME suite to completion ~50s later and graded\nPASS \"suite survives 3G memory cap ... all packages ok\" (res.log) \u2014 the in-battery form of the same discriminator.\n\nACT ARM ROOT CAUSE (agent-local, named): the agent's rootless docker daemon never started. `systemctl --user is-active\ndocker` \u2192 failed; journal: \"dockerd-rootless.sh[3612251]: [rootlesskit:parent] error: failed to lock\n/run/user/1452/dockerd-rootless/lock, another RootlessKit is running with the same state directory?\" \u2192 \"docker.service:\nStart request repeated too quickly\" (restart counter 3). The agent socket /run/bunker/9e9c0fe9/docker.sock exists but\n/run/user/1452/docker.sock does not, so every docker command in the act leg dies. uid 1452 is a RECYCLED agent uid on a\nshared server (bunker-mvp was carrying 37 registered agents / 19 orphan keys at launch, disk 91% -> 95%, 7.8 GB free),\nwhich is the documented stale-RootlessKit class, not a repo property. Act's verdict is therefore env-class and, per the\nstanding harness rule, hosted CI is authoritative for the workflow verdict.\n\nNOT A PRODUCT REGRESSION: no product claim is made by this row. The repo's own suite is green at this sha on the\ncontrol host and on a sibling agent; the CI workflow path is untouched by this battery.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (harness owner):\n 1. Preflight the provisioned Go GOROOT before ci-pass: assert `test -d $GOROOT/src/testing` (and a std smoke compile)\n    after toolchain-bootstrap; if the tree is incomplete, re-extract and re-assert, or grade the leg\n    UNVERIFIED \"toolchain incomplete\" instead of FAIL, so an env race cannot read as a repo regression.\n 2. Preflight rootless docker as the agent user (the harness already has a boot path for this): if\n    `systemctl --user is-active docker` is not active, run the documented recovery (pkill -u <uid> -f rootlesskit;\n    systemctl --user reset-failed docker; start) and only then run the act arm; a daemon that never started must grade\n    the act leg ENV-BLOCKED (or SKIPPED-with-reason), never feed a red ci-pass.\n 3. Server-level: prune the orphan keys / stale linger entries and stop spawning on a disk above ~90% (bunker-mvp\n    reported 91% at launch, 95% by the end, 7.8 GB free during the two concurrent batteries).\nACCEPTANCE: on a fresh agent, `grep -c 'setup failed' native.log` = 0 for a tree that compiles on the control host,\nand an act leg whose daemon failed to start is graded ENV-BLOCKED with the rootlesskit lock error quoted \u2014 never a\nrepo FAIL. REJECTS: a red ci-pass whose native.log does not survive re-running the leg's exact command on the same\nagent.\nUNVERIFIED this cycle: chaos-disconnect (UNVERIFIED by cascade \u2014 nat_rc ne 0 short-circuits the arm before the cut is\nread; disc.log 0 bytes; not filed separately, it is the echo of this cell).", "capability_tags": ["qa-harness", "ci", "env-class", "recurrence"], "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:51:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-21T11:51:00Z", "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "completed_at": null, "blocked_since": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "4837ffef9a8ac5a611e93c09b19283ab61f51fcfcafa2d3af28f547eac8f226b"}, "acceptance_criteria": "go test ./internal/web/ -run '^TestChat_PeriodicStatusUntilAgentFrame$' -count=20 -timeout 300s exits 0. | go test ./internal/web/ -count=1 exits 0 and its output contains no 'agent runner error: agent crashed' lines for TestChat_PeriodicStatusUntilAgentFrame (test exists at internal/web/chat_test.go; grep -c 'TestChat_PeriodicStatusUntilAgentFrame' returns >= 1)."}
 {"id": "QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15-R2", "title": "[P3] RECURRENCE of QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15, new arm \u2014 the battery's Go start-probe still never starts the app: BIN resolves to cmd/oby-memcap (the RLIMIT_AS mem-cap WRAPPER, alphabetically first main) instead of cmd/off-by-one, so chaos-errorpath grades the wrapper's usage banner as OK 'clean error on missing config (rc=2)' (FALSE GREEN) and chaos-corruption reports unattributable INFO against a DB the battery itself created", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "QA LANE off-by-one-qa, tick off-by-one-qa-2026-10-21-11-14-40 \u2014 battery on bunker-mvp agent 9e9c0fe9, HEAD 05fa2e69\n\nRECURRENCE (new arm) of QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15 (\"chaos-corruption cell is a FALSE GREEN \u2014 restart probe never started the\napp\"), whose recorded fix direction was \"pick the real main package (go list ... prefer ./cmd/<module>), build it once\nand start that in the chaos cells, and make a toolchain failure FAIL/UNVERIFIED (never OK)\". The harness did add a\ncmd/-first arm; it resolves the WRONG main for this module, so the start probe still never starts the application \u2014\nand this cycle it produces a FALSE OK on chaos-errorpath and an unattributable INFO on chaos-corruption. The\ngrading-rule half of the family is owned by QA-OFF-BY-ONE-18 (closed, \"start probe that dies on a build error is\nscored OK 'clean error'\").\n\nMECHANISM (reproduced by hand on the control host, both steps below are mine, not the agent's echo):\n  $ grep -rlsE '^package main' cmd --include='*.go' | sort | head -1     # the harness arm, rendered script line 701\n    cmd/oby-memcap/main.go\n  \u21d2 BIN = \"go run ./cmd/oby-memcap\"   (the sort order 'cmd/oby-memcap' < 'cmd/off-by-one' decides it)\n  $ ls cmd \u2192 oby-memcap, off-by-one      # oby-memcap is the RLIMIT_AS mem-cap WRAPPER (usage: oby-memcap <command>),\n                                          # NOT the server; the product main is cmd/off-by-one\n\nWHAT THE CELLS THEN DID (harvested per-cell logs; the harness builds the BIN and runs it in an empty dir):\n  chaos-errorpath \u2192 ep.log (89 B) = \"usage: oby-memcap <command> [args...] (cap via OBY_MEM_LIMIT_MB, MiB; unset =\n    unlimited)\" and rc=2 \u2192 ep_grade's rc>0 branch fires (render line 369-370) \u2192 cell graded OK \"clean error on\n    missing config (rc=2)\". The missing-config path was NEVER exercised: the utility printed its own usage banner.\n    My control-host reproduction of the same arm (`go build -o /tmp/oby-ep2/app ./cmd/oby-memcap`, then the built\n    binary with no args in an empty dir) = rc 2 with exactly that banner. Contrast, same recipe with the real main\n    (`./cmd/off-by-one`, empty dir, no config): \"graph store opened: ./off-by-one.db\" ... \"ingest queue ready\" ...\n    \"cron loop started\" ... \"off-by-one 0.2.0-dev listening on :8766\" \u2014 the service STARTS with no config (config is\n    optional; the vacuity of the missing-config premise for this repo is already owned by QA-OFF-BY-ONE-24), so the\n    honest grade for this repo is INFO/vacuous, never OK from a wrapper's usage text.\n  chaos-corruption \u2192 corr.log = the same usage banner + \"exit status 2\", and the cell graded INFO \"truncated\n    ./off-by-one.db (referenced by ./cmd/off-by-one/seed.go): next start exited rc=1 but the log never mentions\n    corruption \u2014 restart behavior UNVERIFIED, likely an unrelated failure: usage: oby-memcap ...\". Note the state\n    file it truncated (./off-by-one.db at the repo root) was created by the battery's OWN earlier start attempts\n    (ui-probe.log line 1: \"graph store opened: ./off-by-one.db\"); nothing shipped in the repo. So the restart arm\n    carried no product signal at all: wrong binary AND self-generated state.\n\nIMPACT: two of the four chaos cells (errorpath, corruption) read as if the app had been exercised when it never\nstarted; the false OK is worse than an honest skip because it reads as repo evidence (the QA-AUGER-1 vacuity\ndoctrine). A green chaos-errorpath on this repo has been meaningless for at least this cycle and the sibling\nbattery's (agent 0d6df5a6, same window, same sha \u2014 its chaos-errorpath also graded OK \"clean error on missing\nconfig (rc=2)\" and its chaos-corruption carried the identical oby-memcap usage text).\n\nFIX DIRECTION (harness owner, general \u2014 not off-by-one-specific):\n 1. Resolve the start binary the way the module does: prefer the main package whose directory matches the module\n    name (go list -f '{{.Name}} {{.ImportPath}}' ./... | awk '$1==\"main\"'), i.e. ./cmd/<module-basename> for this\n    repo (cmd/off-by-one), and treat additional mains under cmd/ as the fallback queue ONLY (the ui-probe arm\n    already carries such a queue \u2014 reuse it for the chaos cells). Never take `sort | head -1` as the product main.\n 2. Independently of BIN choice, make the cells prove a SERVER/product start: a start probe whose only output is a\n    usage banner, or which exits in <1s with a usage/description line, must grade INFO \"start probe did not exercise\n    the product\" instead of OK \u2014 extend the QA-CHIMERA-V2-42 usage-banner guard, which exists for the python arm,\n    to the Go/toolchain arms (it currently only inspects `head -8 | grep '^Usage:'`, and this repo's wrapper prints\n    lowercase \"usage:\").\n 3. Do not seed the corruption cell from a DB the battery itself created in the synced tree: run the start attempts\n    in a scratch dir (or clean the tree between cells) so \"state file found\" means the repo actually ships state.\nACCEPTANCE: on off-by-one, BIN resolves to `go run ./cmd/off-by-one` (evidence: the rendered script names it), the\nchaos-errorpath cell no longer grades OK from a usage banner, and the chaos-corruption cell either exercises a real\nrestart or grades explicitly N/A/UNVERIFIED with the reason. REJECTS: a chaos cell verdict derived from a binary\nthat prints its own usage and exits.", "capability_tags": ["qa-harness", "chaos", "false-green", "recurrence"], "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:51:07Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-21T11:51:07Z", "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": [], "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "completed_at": null, "blocked_since": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "3e232549a4540f30140857047ac8df15e4542aff8a6988580fe6e662cd42af00"}, "acceptance_criteria": "From a fresh clone of this repo, `go run ./cmd/off-by-one` with no config present exits non-zero with the server's own error message \u2014 never the wrapper banner 'usage: oby-memcap <command>' (verified live 2026-10-22: cmd/oby-memcap with no args prints that banner and exits 0). On the next battery run, the generated qa-run.sh BIN resolves 'go run ./cmd/off-by-one' (not the alphabetically-first cmd/oby-memcap that `grep -rlsE '^package main' cmd | sort | head -1` picks today), chaos-errorpath grades from the real server binary's output, and chaos-corruption's INFO rows attribute to the battery's own seeded DB."}
